WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.170
Breccia contains angular large clasts in a finer matrix and is

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.590
commonly poorly sorted. Massive lenses or wedges may have little visible

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:13.450
bedding because material arrived in a sudden chaotic event.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.450
Some fragments remain shattered but close together.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:21.110
These observations support limited rounding, but do not identify one unique

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:21.550
environment.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:26.230
Mudflows and debris flows carry mixtures down steep slopes.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.670
Landslides shatter rock during movement.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Streams can build coarse alluvial fans at a mountain front, and

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.350
glaciers can leave mixtures of large fragments and fine rock flour.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:40.470
Breccia is compatible with several of these settings, so inspect matrix,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.590
geometry and surrounding deposits.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:47.250
Conglomerate has rounded gravel-sized clasts in sand or mud.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.370
Some beds have many touching clasts and little matrix;

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.270
others contain scattered gravel within finer material.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.030
Rounding usually records abrasion and reworking.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:00.810
Smaller gravel can reflect weaker flow, a finer source, long abrasion

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.550
or a combination of those factors.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.350
Energetic streams and braided channels can deposit coarse gravel.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:10.110
Repeated wave pounding can round beach stones without moving them a

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.330
great distance away. Rounded clasts therefore do not supply one exact

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:18.290
travel distance. Match the rock with channel forms, shoreline evidence and

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.390
other observations before choosing its environment.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:25.290
Conglomerate can also occur in deltas and underwater flows near continental

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:30.070
slopes. Large clasts show that an effective transporting or moving process

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.010
was available; the setting need not have been dry land.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:37.510
Breccia and conglomerate share coarse grain size, while angular versus rounded

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:39.150
clasts distinguish their names.
